Alsayf imports the seven upstream cli mode packages and their discovery engines
through github.com/OJ/gobuster/v3, pinned in go.mod/go.sum. Upstream runtime
sources are not copied or modified. The upstream LICENSE is preserved here.

The local cmd/gobuster and internal/gobuster adapters create a fresh upstream
command tree, preserve native flags, propagate the Alsayf cancellation context,
and return CLI framework errors to the root command. They add argument, worker
count, delay, and timeout validation before invoking mode handlers.

The standalone upstream main function, its process exit handling, its global
version-printer override, and its automatic GOMAXPROCS adjustment are not used.
Upstream scan output uses process standard streams, and inherited logger fatal
paths can terminate the process on output errors. Wordlists are supplied by the
user and are not bundled or downloaded by Alsayf.
